---
<Layout pageTitle="Spin coating laboratory" subtitle="" description="Operate a reference-informed Laurell WS-650Mz spin coater and generate an empirical photoresist thickness map.">
<article class="equipment eq-sheet spin" id="spin">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/02-07/">← Equipment 02-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#spin-evidence">Evidence &amp; verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">02-07 / PHOTORESIST PROCESSING / V1.0</span><h2>Laurell WS-650Mz-23NPPB</h2><p>650-series tabletop spin coater · standard Mz motor · natural polypropylene · clear lid and 1.75-inch vacuum chuck. Educational metric reconstruction, not manufacturer CAD or equipment control.</p></header>
<div class="spin-grid">
<section><div class="spin-head"><strong>01 / Instrument</strong><span id="spin-state">UNLOADED</span></div><div id="spin-view" aria-label="Interactive 3D spin coater"><p id="spin-loading">Loading instrument geometry…</p></div>
<div class="spin-buttons">{['whole','front','side','rear','bowl','controller'].map(view=><button type="button" data-spin-view={view}>{view==='whole'?'Reset view':view}</button>)}<button type="button" id="spin-glb" disabled>Export GLB</button></div>
<p class="small">Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. Open lid to inspect the bowl. Film thickness and rotation speed are exaggerated or slowed visually, not to scale in those respects.</p>
<p id="spin-model-status" role="status">Loading glTF…</p><p><a href={base+'laurell.gltf'} download>Download glTF</a> · <a href={base+'laurell.glb'} download>Download GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model-source.mjs'} download>Editable model source</a></p>
</section>
<section><div class="spin-head"><strong>02 / Process controller</strong><span>AZ 1512</span></div>
<div class="spin-buttons"><button type="button" id="spin-example">Run ready example</button><button type="button" id="spin-reset">Reset</button><button type="button" id="spin-lid">Open lid</button><button type="button" id="spin-load">Load wafer</button><button type="button" id="spin-vacuum">Vacuum on</button><button type="button" id="spin-dispense">Dispense resist</button><button type="button" id="spin-start">Start recipe</button><button type="button" id="spin-stop" disabled>Abort</button><button type="button" id="spin-unload">Unload</button></div>
<p id="spin-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Load wafer with lid open, secure vacuum, dispense and close the lid, then run. Or run the ready example.</p>
<progress id="spin-progress" max="1" value="0" aria-label="Accelerated recipe progress"></progress>
<div class="spin-readouts"><span>Time <strong id="spin-time">0.0 s</strong></span><span>Speed <strong id="spin-current-rpm">0 rpm</strong></span><span>Vacuum <strong id="spin-vac-state">OFF</strong></span></div>
<div class="spin-fields">{fields.map(([id,label,type,value,min,max,step])=><label>{label}<input id={'spin-'+id} type={type} value={value} min={min} max={max} step={step}/></label>)}</div>
<label class="spin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="spin-utility" checked/> Vacuum supply and purge available (simulated)</label>
<p><label>Import job JSON <input type="file" id="spin-import" accept=".json,application/json"/></label> · <a href={base+'example-job.json'} download>Example input</a></p>
<p class="small">The 2 mm centering and coverage thresholds are teaching assumptions; no actual safety limits or fluid volume recipe implied. Hold duration, acceleration and dispense affect validity and recorded history, not the fitted steady film thickness.</p>
</section></div>
<section><div class="spin-head"><strong>03 / Resist-layer revision</strong><span>SIMULATED · NOT MEASURED</span></div><div class="spin-results">
<figure><figcaption>Wafer thickness map (µm)</figcaption><canvas id="spin-map" width="324" height="324" aria-label="Thickness map"></canvas><p id="spin-legend">Run a recipe to populate map.</p><p id="spin-probe">Tap or move over the map for local coordinates.</p></figure>
<figure><figcaption>Recipe speed vs elapsed time</figcaption><canvas id="spin-chart" width="480" height="280" aria-label="Recipe speed history"></canvas><p id="spin-readout" aria-live="polite">No committed resist revision.</p></figure></div>
<div class="spin-buttons"><button type="button" id="spin-json" disabled>Export resist revision JSON</button><button type="button" id="spin-csv" disabled>Export map CSV</button><a href={base+'example-resist-layer.json'} download>Example handoff</a><a href={base+'output-schema.json'} download>Output schema</a><a href={base+'solver.mjs'} download>Numerical source</a></div>
<p>Handoff contract: bts.spin-coater.resist-layer.v1 retains sample and contact IDs, parent and child revisions, material/calibration, centering, time history and a wafer-centered thickness grid in µm. The map is row-major +Z from the back of the wafer; origin is (-R,-R) in mm and null denotes outside the wafer. No compatible consumer adapter is claimed; the example and schema document the proposed next-station handoff.</p></section>
<section id="spin-evidence"><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>Selected installed 23NPPB configuration, related current 23NPP manufacturer specification and 10077303 Rev C on-deck drawing. External photos and drawing are linked, not republished, because reuse rights have not been established. The original orthographic mesh renders below use the actual downloadable geometry; they are not photographs. Front, bowl and rear-side views were inspected against corresponding installed-machine photographs. Use matching inspection views above.</p>
<div class="spin-refs">
<figure><img src={base+'reference-front.png'} alt="Closed front view of generated Laurell spin coater" width="540" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>{diagrams[0][1]} <a href={diagrams[0][2]}>Montana State installed front</a>; <a href={brochure+'#page=1'}>manufacturer p. 1</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={base+'reference-open-bowl.png'} alt="Generated bowl and vacuum chuck with lid open" width="540" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>{diagrams[1][1]} <a href={diagrams[1][2]}>CU Boulder photo</a>; <a href={sop+'#page=2'}>Arizona SOP, operation</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={base+'reference-rear-side.png'} alt="Generated rear-side view of drain and utility connectors" width="540" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>{diagrams[2][1]} <a href={diagrams[2][2]}>23NPP side and keypad photos</a>; <a href={drawing}>dimensional drawing Rev C</a>.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Comparison: the closed front reproduces the cylindrical enclosure, front latch and right-side tilted 650 controller with a blue display; keypad legends, seam details and logo treatment are simplified. The open bowl reproduces the central chuck and rear hinge; the lid top is cropped to emphasize the working area and the lid skirt and bowl depth remain estimated. The related rear-side photo supports a drain cup and hinged enclosure; rear port locations, hose routes and cup proportions are inferred, not measured. These checks establish qualitative resemblance only.</p>
<h3>Specifications and assumptions</h3><div class="spin-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{specs.map(([label,value,meaning,url])=><tr><td>{label}</td><td>{value}</td><td>{meaning}</td><td>{url?<a href={url}>Reference</a>:'Assumed'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<h3>Numerical model</h3><p>Fit log(thickness) against log(rpm/1000) using seven approximate Merck graph points (500–3500 rpm). The resulting thickness is h = 2.7143 (rpm/1000)<sup>−0.5166</sup> µm. The 4000 rpm point was withheld. This is an empirical final-film correlation, not a transient Navier–Stokes or evaporation solver. It assumes conditions comparable to the graph, for which the exact bake, spin time, and metrology protocol are unspecified. Extrapolation outside the speed domain is blocked. Other wafer sizes are explicitly unvalidated.</p>
<p>For each wafer-centered position X,Z, r = √(X²+Z²), R = wafer radius, the illustrative spatial thickness is h × [1+A exp(−(R−r)/w)] × [1+0.04(offsetX × X + offsetZ × Z)/(2R)]. A and w set the bead amplitude and width. The asymmetry coefficient and bead terms are chosen teaching parameters, not measured fits. Acceleration is a linear speed ramp; rotation display is time compressed. Volume and dwell are recipe constraints/history only. Neither absolute edge thickness nor centering-induced uniformity is validated.</p>
<h3>Verification</h3><p>Independent numerical reference checks executed before integration. The manufacturer's held-out point is a digitized graph value (±0.15 µm graph-reading tolerance, roughly three pixels), not a raw measurement with reported uncertainty. The Montana State comparison is independent but the reported ±0.476 µm is not characterized as measurement uncertainty. Thus the equipment register's strict measured holdout acceptance is only partially satisfied. Geometry checks compare encoded nominal scales, not dimensional metrology. Browser/CI results are tracked separately.</p>
<div class="spin-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Units</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[...verification.numerical,...verification.geometry].map(row=><tr><td>{row.test}</td><td>{Number(row.expected.toFixed(6))}</td><td>{Number(row.actual.toFixed(6))}</td><td>{row.unit}</td><td>{row.tolerance}</td><td>{row.pass?'PASS':'FAIL'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p><a href={base+'verification.json'} download>Verification data</a> · <a href={curve+'#page=1'}>Merck curve, p. 1</a> · <a href={independent}>Montana State AZ 1512 procedure</a>.</p>
</section>
</article>
